This issue seems like it is a result of the arm package having a method named "sim". A work around may be to simply specify which method you would like to use. Try the following:

  s.out <- Zelig:::sim(z.out2, x=x.low, x1=x.high,num=10000)

I will do a little more investigation into the matter, and see if there are non-work-around solutions available. The situation is slightly complicated by the fact that arm:::sim is a method of an S4 object and Zelig:::sim is a method for S3 objects.

- Matt Owen

